message: "If you use this workflow or code in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "enhancer-gene-atac-rna-ctcf: Reproducible Snakemake workflow for ATAC-seq, RNA-seq, and CTCF enhancer-gene integration"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
url: "https://arjunbioinfo.github.io/"
# Add repository-code and doi fields once pushed to GitHub and archived on Zenodo.
authors:
  - family-names: "Thippana"
    given-names: "Mallikarjuna"
    affiliation: "Department of Oncology-Pathology, Karolinska Institutet"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - epigenomics
  - ATAC-seq
  - RNA-seq
  - CTCF
  - enhancer-gene regulation
  - Snakemake
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  A config-driven Snakemake and Python pipeline that integrates ATAC-seq chromatin
  accessibility, RNA-seq gene expression, and CTCF ChIP-seq occupancy to link distal
  enhancers to target genes, test CTCF regulatory enrichment, and prioritize
  candidate regulatory loci using public ENCODE GRCh38 datasets.
